# Containers on AWS AWS Whitepaper

> This whitepaper provides guidance and options for running Docker on AWS. Docker is an open platform for developing, shipping, and running applications in a loosely isolated environment called a container. Amazon Web Services (AWS) is a natural complement to containers and offers a wide range of scalable infrastructure services upon which containers can be deployed. You will find various options such as AWS Elastic Beanstalk, Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS), AWS Fargate, and AWS App Runner. This paper cover details of each option and key components of the container orchestration.

